  "query_preview": "..(Monday through Saturday)\nIssued at 354 PM EDT SAT OCT 17 2026\n\nThe models are in good agreement for the long-term period. This \ncomes as upper-level ridging builds toward the Ohio Valley. At the \nsurface, we will remain under the control of passing surface high \npressure systems for the period. The biggest impacts on the horizon \nfor the week will be the possibility of frost Monday morning and \nagain Monday night into Tuesday, confined primarily to the sheltered \nvalleys. Outside of the frosty mornings to start the week, expect \nafternoon highs to moderate, climbing back toward the 70s as the \nperiod progresses.",
